-- =============================================================================
-- Dalaran Underbelly -> map 1413 (guild house)
-- =============================================================================
-- Retail keeps Legion Dalaran's sewers on their own map (1502) that the modern
-- client seamlessly swaps to. We need NO such script: our dalaran2.wmo already
-- contains the Underbelly (WMO area groups 7594 The Underbelly / 7825 Underbelly
-- Descent / 8011 Hall of Shadows / 8012 Chamber of Shadows), which is why the
-- well teleporter already drops players into a real sewer.
--
-- Proof the geometry lines up: pushing retail map-1502 spawns through the SAME
-- fitted transform used for the city puts the Underbelly population at z ~499-500,
-- and the well teleporter's exit is z 499.26. Hall of Shadows rows land at z ~398,
-- matching the Khadgar we already have down there at z 400.8.
--   x' = -0.77746771*x - -0.62892286*y + -2364.3865
--   y' = -0.62892286*x + -0.77746771*y + 4021.6060
--   z' = z -203.1140
--
-- 219 of 266 retail sewer spawns are imported. What is NOT imported:
--   * named Legion characters and class-hall NPCs (Madam Goya, Ms. Xiulan, the
--     Black Harvest warlocks, Raethan, ...) - their retail models do not exist in
--     our client, and dressing them in stock models would look wrong. They need a
--     proper model downport first.
--   * the Ratstallion taxi vehicle (needs vehicle seat data) and summoning portals.
--   * ALL gameobjects. The 71 true Underbelly objects (Underbelly Cache/Spoils/
--     Hoard, Shimmering Whorl, candles) use GO displays 18020/17863/25466/12441/
--     ... which are absent from our GameObjectDisplayInfo -- they need a GO model
--     downport of their own. (The other 352 map-1502 objects are duplicates of
--     city props we already imported from map 1220.)
--
-- Ambient creatures whose retail model is missing are given a fitting stock
-- display instead (mostly from WotLK's own Dalaran sewers) - see the comment on
-- each template below.
--
-- FACTION: every imported NPC is set to faction 35 (friendly, non-combat), the
-- same convention the city import used. Retail's Underbelly is a hostile
-- free-for-all zone; inside a guild house that would be hostile mobs attacking
-- guild members, so they are ambience only. Change `faction` here if you want it
-- faithful to retail instead.
--
-- Every spawn INSERT is guarded by a NOT EXISTS position check, so re-running
-- this file - or having imported some of it another way - can never produce
-- duplicate spawns.
--
-- Requires a worldserver restart.
-- =============================================================================

